\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Nine documented multi-stablecoin de-peg episodes over 2020--2025 and their wall-type assignments. Wall types as in \S  \ref {sec:walltypes}; assignment follows the primary structural failure in the regulator and post-mortem literature (Appendix~\ref {app:data}). USDC-SVB is a triple wall following \citet  {MaZengZhang2023}. The rightmost column reports whether the event delivers a multi-coin wall-affected block or a single-coin block. Only 3 of the 9 events deliver a multi-coin wall-affected block, and the pair-level gradient test of \S  \ref {sec:gradient} is defined on exactly those three; the remaining six are single-coin blocks and cannot carry the test by construction (\S  \ref {sec:single}).}}{17}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:events}{{1}{17}{Nine documented multi-stablecoin de-peg episodes over 2020--2025 and their wall-type assignments. Wall types as in \S \ref {sec:walltypes}; assignment follows the primary structural failure in the regulator and post-mortem literature (Appendix~\ref {app:data}). USDC-SVB is a triple wall following \citet {MaZengZhang2023}. The rightmost column reports whether the event delivers a multi-coin wall-affected block or a single-coin block. Only 3 of the 9 events deliver a multi-coin wall-affected block, and the pair-level gradient test of \S \ref {sec:gradient} is defined on exactly those three; the remaining six are single-coin blocks and cannot carry the test by construction (\S \ref {sec:single})}{table.1}{}}
